{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1255825-are-mummies-immortal-or-not","id":1255825,"title":"Are Mummies immortal or not?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-20T12:03:29-07:00","id":1255825,"title":"Are Mummies immortal or not?","content":"According to the Aging paragraph in chapter 5 of the M:TR core book (p.135) Mummies do not age, but at the same time the Ba Background (p.64) grants extra decades of life to the Mummy. So are Mummies immortal or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T15:06:42-07:00","id":1255912,"title":"","content":"Depends how you want to define immortal I guess.<br /> <br /> Mummies don't age, but they have a limited amount of time &quot;alive&quot; in the physical world before they need to die and spend time in the underworld. But they get to come back after that.<br /> <br /> So... it's a matter of perspective. They don't live forever and can die, but they also auto-self resurrect. Are you immortal if you die and come back over and over? If yes, then yes they are. If no, they're not... but they're something close to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T02:08:18-07:00","id":1256039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1255825-are-mummies-immortal-or-not?p=1255912#post1255912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummies don't age, but they have a limited amount of time &quot;alive&quot; in the physical world before they need to die and spend time in the underworld. But they get to come back after that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the only thing that implies this is the Ba Background. As for the rest, Mummies are both unaging and can be reborn if they are killed through violence. Or is this contradicted elsewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T02:57:22-07:00","id":1256046,"title":"","content":"I don't remember if it got clarified elsewhere, but yeah, Ba is the only place that details it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"